    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>&quot;Can you reach Level 0?&quot;</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Trapped in a decaying high-rise, you must descend. The body in the hallway is proof that something has gone terribly wrong. The stairs loop endlessly\u2014each floor shifting, rewriting itself. Some things are real. Some are not. <strong>Find the anomalies. Escape before the system corrects you.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Neuromira is a <strong>survival horror game with psychological and digital horror elements</strong>. Inspired by classic <strong>pre-rendered horror games of the late \u201890s</strong>, it blends a suffocating cyber-atmosphere with glitching realities and an unfolding mystery.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>\ud83d\udd37 Features</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udd79 <strong>Point &amp; Click Survival Horror</strong> \u2013 Solve puzzles, evade the system\u2019s corrections, and descend deeper into the truth.<br>\ud83d\udda5 <strong>Digital Decay Aesthetic</strong> \u2013 A mix of retro-futuristic visuals, VHS artifacts, and corrupted data.<br>\ud83c\udfad <strong>Unstable NPCs</strong> \u2013 Each floor holds a resident\u2014or what\u2019s left of them. Some help, some hinder, all are trapped.<br>\ud83d\udd04 <strong>The Loop Watches You</strong> \u2013 Make the wrong move, and the simulation resets\u2026 with something different this time.<br>\ud83e\udde9 <strong>Unravel the Hidden Reality</strong> \u2013 Read corrupted logs, hack forgotten terminals, and piece together the story of <strong>Vanir Corp\u2019s</strong> final experiment.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Descend carefully. <strong>The building is not just breaking\u2014it\u2019s watching.</strong></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>&quot;Can you reach Level 0?&quot;</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Trapped in a decaying high-rise, you must descend. The body in the hallway is proof that something has gone terribly wrong. The stairs loop endlessly\u2014each floor shifting, rewriting itself. Some things are real. Some are not. <strong>Find the anomalies. Escape before the system corrects you.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Neuromira is a <strong>survival horror game with psychological and digital horror elements</strong>. Inspired by classic <strong>pre-rendered horror games of the late \u201890s</strong>, it blends a suffocating cyber-atmosphere with glitching realities and an unfolding mystery.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>\ud83d\udd37 Features</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udd79 <strong>Point &amp; Click Survival Horror</strong> \u2013 Solve puzzles, evade the system\u2019s corrections, and descend deeper into the truth.<br>\ud83d\udda5 <strong>Digital Decay Aesthetic</strong> \u2013 A mix of retro-futuristic visuals, VHS artifacts, and corrupted data.<br>\ud83c\udfad <strong>Unstable NPCs</strong> \u2013 Each floor holds a resident\u2014or what\u2019s left of them. Some help, some hinder, all are trapped.<br>\ud83d\udd04 <strong>The Loop Watches You</strong> \u2013 Make the wrong move, and the simulation resets\u2026 with something different this time.<br>\ud83e\udde9 <strong>Unravel the Hidden Reality</strong> \u2013 Read corrupted logs, hack forgotten terminals, and piece together the story of <strong>Vanir Corp\u2019s</strong> final experiment.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Descend carefully. <strong>The building is not just breaking\u2014it\u2019s watching.</strong></p>",
